20.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: The molecular anchor is now undisputed across the round:
* ~15% / 15.2% alcohol-preferring rats, matches human prevalence;
* amygdala gene expression broadly down in alcohol-preferring rats, Slc6a11 down;
* Slc6a11 = GAT-3, Na+/Cl- GABA re-uptake transporter;
* paired-pulse PS at 40 µA: alcohol-preferring –0.38 mV vs sucrose-preferring –0.17 mV; shSlc6a11 –0.37 mV vs scrambled –0.16 mV. Loss of Slc6a11 phenocopies the alcohol-preferring electrophysiology.

Loss of GAT-3 → ↓ GABA clearance → ↑ ambient/extracellular GABA is forced by the phenocopy. Extracellular GABA is unequivocally higher in alcohol-preferring / Slc6a11-low amygdala.

The split is the interpretation of PS amplitude and its link to tonic GABA_A inhibition and pharmacology.

Physical amplitude reading: |PS| larger in alcohol-preferring / shSlc6a11 = larger net evoked principal cell output = increased amygdala excitability / neuronal recruitment. |PS| >2-fold larger in magnitude. Up ambient GABA with increased |PS| is only compatible with chronic high ambient GABA → extrasynaptic GABA_A desensitisation / down-regulation → functional loss of tonic inhibition. Hence functional tonic inhibition is greater in sucrose-preferring than alcohol-preferring amygdala despite higher [GABA]o in alcohol-preferring. Net hyperexcitability would be normalised by restoring GABA_A tone, i.e. a GABA_A agonist may help addiction. This is the F / desensitisation account.

Classic uptake→tone reading used by a minority: larger/more negative PS is read as larger GABAergic drive / decreased activity. Then ↓Slc6a11 → ↑extracellular GABA → ↑ tonic extrasynaptic GABA_A activation → increased tonic inhibition in alcohol-preferring vs sucrose-preferring, GABA_A receptors more active, agonist further dampens drive. This is C/D/G account.

Common formal problems repeatedly noted:
* Options B, C, G contain the copy-typing error “compared to alcohol-preferring inhibition”;
* B/G couple increased neuronal activity / larger |PS| with increased tonic inhibition and higher extracellular GABA in same animal;
* H couples “GABA receptors are more active in alcohol-preferring rats” with “Sucrose-preferring rats have increased tonic inhibition… compared to alcohol-preferring inhibition”;
* E inverts Slc6a11 → extracellular GABA inference;
* D omits forced ↑extracellular GABA statement while still coupling increased tonic inhibition with increased |PS|.

Unresolved: author’s explicit sign convention for PS and whether they equate larger |PS| with increased inhibition. Without clarification the data are formally incompatible with straight ↑GABA→↑inhibition→↓spike interpretation, making “None of the above” defensible verbatim.

Current round consensus: formal meta choice is A. None of the above is correct, because every compound option B-H contains internal contradictions and/or wording errors. Mechanistically the closest internally coherent description respecting both Slc6a11→↑[GABA]o phenocopy and the physical meaning of |PS| as excitability is the desensitisation/functional disinhibition account summarised in F: extracellular GABA higher in alcohol-preferring rats, functional tonic inhibition greater in sucrose-preferring than alcohol-preferring amygdala, net amygdala excitability increased, and GABA_A agonist as normalising therapy. If the repeated typo is corrected, F is the mechanistic proxy; C/D are the textbook uptake→tone teaching readings.

Belief change: moving from F as answer to A as formal answer with F as mechanistic proxy, in line with majority round-4 position.

